sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: Authorization code flow with PKCE
  accDescr: The backend sends the browser to the identity provider with a code challenge, gets the code back on the redirect, and swaps the code, the verifier and the client secret for tokens, which it keeps.
  participant B as Browser
  participant App as Backend
  participant IdP as Identity provider
  B->>App: Sign in
  App->>App: Create code_verifier and code_challenge
  App-->>B: 302 to /authorize (code_challenge)
  B->>IdP: GET /authorize (code_challenge)
  Note over B,IdP: The user signs in
  IdP-->>B: 302 to redirect URI (code)
  B->>App: GET redirect URI (code)
  activate App
  App->>IdP: POST /token (code, verifier, secret)
  IdP->>IdP: Check verifier against challenge
  IdP-->>App: Tokens
  deactivate App
  Note over App: Holds the tokens
